{% elsif page_key == 'manufacturing' %}
<section class="rd-sec rd-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="narrow">
<p class="kicker">How it is made</p>
<h1>Wound, pocketed,<br>stacked, closed.</h1>
<p class="lede">Nothing is built before somebody orders it. Every mattress starts as wire on a spool and ends as a roll in a box, and both of those happen after you have chosen your size.</p>
</div></div>
<div class="wrap" style="margin-top:60px"><figure class="figure ">{% render 'rd-video', file: 'spring.mp4', poster: 'spring-poster.webp', video_id: 'spring', alt: 'Factory footage' %}<figcaption>On the line &middot; Springs wound and pocketed</figcaption></figure></div>
</section>

<section class="rd-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="narrow">
<div class="sec-head"><p class="kicker">The core</p><h2>Seven zones,<br>two wire gauges.</h2></div>
<p>The spring unit is wound from steel wire on the factory floor, then each spring is sealed into its own fabric pocket so it can move without dragging its neighbours with it.</p>
<p>Ours is arranged in seven zones along the length of the bed. Heavier two millimetre wire sits under the hips and shoulders where load concentrates. One point eight millimetre runs everywhere else. That is why the bed holds a spine level rather than letting the heaviest part of a body sink first.</p>
<div class="pull"><p>Twenty centimetres of springs, each one working on its own.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rd-sec rd-sec--bone"><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-head narrow" style="text-align:center"><p class="kicker">Materials</p><h2>What goes in</h2>
<p class="lede" style="margin:16px auto 0;max-width:36em">Chosen for what they do over a decade, not for what they cost in a year.</p></div>
<div class="matgrid">
<div><p class="k">Cover</p><h3>400 gram cool-knit</h3><p>Knitted rather than laminated, so air moves through the surface instead of being held against it. Zipped the whole way round.</p></div>
<div><p class="k">Comfort</p><h3>Gel-infused memory foam</h3><p>Twenty eight density, the highest in the build. Gel infusion is what lets it contour without holding heat.</p></div>
<div><p class="k">Airflow</p><h3>Wave-profile foam</h3><p>Cut into a wave rather than left flat, so channels run through the middle of the comfort stack and warmth has somewhere to go.</p></div>
<div><p class="k">Support</p><h3>Pocket spring steel</h3><p>Two wire gauges, 1.8 and 2.0 millimetre, wound and pocketed in house. Seven zones along the bed.</p></div>
<div><p class="k">Edge</p><h3>Encased perimeter foam</h3><p>Thirty five density, seven centimetres, wrapped around the entire spring unit so the edge holds when you sit on it.</p></div>
<div><p class="k">Base</p><h3>Anti-slip underside</h3><p>Gripped rather than plain, so the mattress stays where it is put on slats or a divan.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rd-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="narrow">
<div class="sec-head"><p class="kicker">On the bench</p><h2>Assembled by hand</h2></div>
<div class="step"><span class="n">01</span><div><h3>The unit is built</h3>
<p>Springs are wound, pocketed and joined into a single unit at your size. Not cut down from a larger one - built to the dimensions you ordered.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="n">02</span><div><h3>The perimeter is encased</h3>
<p>Thirty five density foam is fitted around the whole spring unit, seven centimetres deep, so the edge behaves like the middle.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="n">03</span><div><h3>The comfort layer is built separately</h3>
<p>Two densities bonded into one ten centimetre layer, medium on one face and medium firm on the other. It is made as its own product, because it has to come out again.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="n">04</span><div><h3>The stack is assembled</h3>
<p>Gel memory foam, comfort foam and wave-profile foam are laid over the comfort layer, and the whole assembly is placed on the core.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="n">05</span><div><h3>The cover is closed</h3>
<p>Cool-knit cover fitted, tape edge finished, zip run the full way round so the comfort layer can be reached without tools.</p></div></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rd-sec rd-sec--dark"><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-head narrow" style="text-align:center"><p class="kicker">Then it is rolled</p><h2>Compressed, so it<br>reaches the room.</h2>
<p class="lede" style="margin:16px auto 0;max-width:36em">A thirty five centimetre mattress does not go up a staircase in one piece. Compression is how it gets there, and it is not how we leave it.</p></div>
<div class="narrow"><figure class="figure ">{% render 'rd-video', file: 'compression.mp4', poster: 'compression-poster.webp', video_id: 'compression', alt: 'Factory footage' %}<figcaption>Compression and roll packing</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="narrow" style="margin-top:40px">
<p style="color:#C9C5BD">Rolled, boxed, and unrolled again on your bed by the people who deliver it. It reaches most of its height within hours and settles fully over the first night.</p>
<p style="color:#C9C5BD">Every piece of packaging leaves with them. So does your old mattress.</p></div>
</div></section>

