{% elsif page_key == 'support' %}
<section class="rd-sec rd-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="hero-split">
<div><p class="kicker">Support</p>
<h1>Support is the core.<br>Comfort is the layer.</h1>
<p class="lede">A back that hurts in the morning is usually a core that has stopped holding. Ours is twenty centimetres of seven-zone pocket springs, guaranteed for twenty five years, with the comfort settled separately.</p>
<div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href="{{ pages['configure'].url | default: '/pages/configure' }}">Choose your size</a><a class="btn btn--ghost btn-line" href="{{ pages['specification'].url | default: '/pages/specification' }}">See the build</a></div></div>
<figure class="figure ">{% render 'rd-img', file: 'product-profile.webp', alt: "Numa mattress in profile", width: 1400, height: 622, loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high' %}</figure>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rd-sec rd-sec--bone"><div class="wrap"><div class="narrow">
<div class="sec-head"><p class="kicker">Two problems</p><h2>Support and comfort are not the same job.</h2></div>
<p>Most mattresses solve both with the same five centimetres, which is why fixing one makes the other worse. Softer for the shoulder means less under the hip. Firmer for the back means pressure at the shoulder.</p>
<div class="pull"><p>Ours separates them. The core holds. The layer adapts.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rd-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-head narrow" style="text-align:center"><p class="kicker">The core</p><h2>Seven zones along the bed</h2>
<p class="lede" style="margin:16px auto 0;max-width:36em">Heavier two millimetre wire under the hips and shoulders. One point eight everywhere else.</p></div>
<div class="split" style="margin-top:52px">
<figure class="figure ">{% render 'rd-img', file: 'coolknit-side.webp', alt: "Side panel over the seven-zone spring core", width: 1400, height: 781, loading: 'lazy' %}</figure>
<div><h3>Why zoning matters for a back</h3>
<p style="margin-top:14px">Your hips are the heaviest part of you and they sink first. On a single-tension mattress that tips the spine out of line for eight hours a night, and you feel it at seven in the morning rather than at eleven at night.</p>
<p>Seven zones put the firmest springs exactly where the load concentrates, so the heaviest part of you is held level with the lightest.</p>
<h3 style="margin-top:30px">Each spring works alone</h3>
<p style="margin-top:14px">Individually pocketed, so movement does not travel. One person turning over does not move the other side of the bed.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rd-sec rd-sec--bone"><div class="wrap"><div class="split rev">
<figure class="figure ">{% render 'rd-img', file: 'product-floating.webp', alt: "The comfort layer above the core", width: 1600, height: 904, loading: 'lazy' %}</figure>
<div><p class="kicker">Adjust to Desire</p><h2>You do not have to get it right.</h2>
<p style="margin-top:20px">Which is fortunate, because nobody can. Firm or soft, medium or medium firm - it is an impossible question to answer in a showroom and a costly one to answer wrong.</p>
<p>So you do not answer it. Every mattress arrives the same. Sleep on it for a month, tell us where it is wrong, and we make a new comfort layer to that description. With our compliments, worth {{ layer_price | default: '£299' }}.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rd-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="narrow">
<div class="sec-head"><h2>Specification</h2></div>
<ul class="spec">
<li><b>Core</b><span>20cm seven-zone pocket springs, 1.8 and 2.0mm wire. Twenty five year guarantee.</span></li>
