<h1>One bed.<br>Two answers.</h1>
<p class="lede">Two mattresses, linked. Each side supported on its own, each comfort layer tailored separately. What suits one of you does not have to be what suits the other.</p>
<div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href="#configure">Choose your size</a><span><span class="addprice" style="font-size:26px">&pound;4,499</span><span class="mono" style="display:block;margin-top:4px">Split King &middot; pair</span></span></div></div>
<figure class="figure ">{% render 'rd-img', file: 'stack-sizes.webp', alt: "Split King units", width: 1600, height: 893, loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high' %}</figure>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rd-sec rd-sec--bone"><div class="wrap"><div class="narrow">
<div class="sec-head"><p class="kicker">Why two</p><h2>Two people rarely want<br>the same bed.</h2></div>
<p>One sleeps hot, one is cold. One has a bad back, one has a bad shoulder. A single mattress makes that a negotiation, and somebody loses it every night for a decade.</p>
<div class="pull"><p>Two halves. Two comfort layers. Neither of you compromises.</p></div>
<p>Each side is a complete mattress with its own seven-zone pocket spring core and its own removable layer. After a month, you each tell us how your side should feel. We make two layers, to two descriptions.</p>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rd-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-head narrow" style="text-align:center"><p class="kicker">How it goes together</p><h2>One surface, two beds</h2></div>
<div class="split" style="margin-top:52px">
<figure class="figure ">{% render 'rd-img', file: 'room-dark.webp', alt: "A split king bed dressed as one", width: 1400, height: 781, loading: 'lazy' %}</figure>
<div><ul class="spec">
<li><b>Linked</b><span>Joined along the inner edge so they behave as one bed and do not drift apart.</span></li>
<li><b>One surface</b><span>Dressed with a single fitted sheet. The join sits between you, not under either of you.</span></li>
<li><b>Two answers</b><span>Each layer is changed on its own. One of you can go softer without the other going with them.</span></li>
<li><b>Any staircase</b><span>Each half rolls and boxes separately, so it reaches rooms a single large mattress cannot.</span></li>
</ul></div></div></div></section>

